WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.848
Households supply labor and demand goods.

2
00:00:02.848 --> 00:00:07.427
Firms differ in productivity and use
production inputs plus fixed operating

3
00:00:07.427 --> 00:00:10.757
labor, with capital rented at a given
price.

4
00:00:12.350 --> 00:00:14.789
Within each sector, Cournot competition

5
00:00:14.789 --> 00:00:18.204
links market shares, elasticities,
markups, and prices.

6
00:00:18.204 --> 00:00:23.570
Relative prices allocate demand across
sectors and among their operating firms.

7
00:00:24.350 --> 00:00:26.931
Output and wages adjust so production

8
00:00:26.931 --> 00:00:30.372
labor plus fixed labor equals household
labor supply.

9
00:00:30.372 --> 00:00:35.533
Profit-based exits change the operating
set, so these conditions are solved again.

10
00:00:36.350 --> 00:00:40.887
Solve two periods separately, each
starting from all potential firms.

11
00:00:40.887 --> 00:00:43.610
Productivity changes, phi stays fixed, and

12
00:00:43.610 --> 00:00:47.240
